                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Ophthalmology teaching is a teaching process that closely follows the foundation of ophthalmology and the development of clinical diagnosis and treatment technology, and needs the basis of optics, psychology, neuroscience, etc., and is closely related to many clinical disciplines. Using multimedia teaching methods, based on the anatomy and physiology of the eyeball and its appendages, combined with ophthalmology special detection and treatment techniques, the epidemiology, disease occurrence, development, clinical manifestation, diagnosis and diagnosis of common eye diseases, especially blind eye diseases. Differential diagnosis, treatment principles and prognosis outcomes for classroom teaching and clinical teaching, and always paying attention to human care and communications.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
